{"id": "EUVD-2026-76279", "enisaUuid": "915275ab-1727-365e-b8a5-0d50b4374ec5", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndm-pcache: only hand out initialized cache segments\n\nget_cache_segment() scans the segment map up to cache->n_segs, the\nphysical device segment count, but cache_segs_init() only initializes\nthe first cache_info->n_segs segments. A crafted image with\ncache_info->n_segs smaller than the device count leaves the remaining\npcache_cache_segment structs zeroed (segment.data == NULL), and the\nallocator can hand one to cache_kset_close(), which writes through the\nreturned segment's data pointer with no NULL check.\n\nBound the allocator's search to cache_info->n_segs so only initialized\nsegments are ever returned. A conforming cache sets n_segs equal to the\ndevice segment count, so this rejects nothing legitimate.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:42:24", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:45:40", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/83e3116283ed2c6a6a1fa662862a4b4d7d2701a2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/692037ae1a7cfacc2f0c22c6e034c1dfee0e553f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2df0fc042e299bae3c0f60ea5cd2af9285658e9f"], "aliases": ["GHSA-2r45-hwhh-3hc3", "CVE-2026-80956"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "04b3f92a-2e91-34ec-986d-dbd3f12c9ab3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1d57628ff95b32d5cfa8d8f50e07690c161e9cf0 <2df0fc042e299bae3c0f60ea5cd2af9285658e9f"}, {"id": "069e2780-1cf4-33d0-93d1-48c173543cb3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.18"}, {"id": "30e21cb1-37cf-3977-8188-b17d12fd4d0c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1d57628ff95b32d5cfa8d8f50e07690c161e9cf0 <83e3116283ed2c6a6a1fa662862a4b4d7d2701a2"}, {"id": "3d8d6d7e-8f35-3c5f-9258-2371ed49b29c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.50"}, {"id": "4326a6f0-f857-32ac-9294-a72fcd6c4209", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1d57628ff95b32d5cfa8d8f50e07690c161e9cf0 <692037ae1a7cfacc2f0c22c6e034c1dfee0e553f"}, {"id": "49cc3451-ca18-314e-bb2b-352529347c45", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "4d9cef35-0a2a-34c9-8900-564ec6e56316", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.4"}, {"id": "58a7368c-8a5d-3332-9d08-4e24d85cfc12", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "63b7b933-5c32-3c08-a351-fae06e5a9be7", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}